{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>This is the Torah for every plague of tzara'at</b> — that is, the tzara'at of a שְׁחִין (boil) and of a מִכְוָה (burn). He mentioned them here first because of their frequency, and afterward He mentioned the נֶתֶק (scall), which is also common, and afterward He mentioned the tzara'at of a garment and of a house, and afterward He said, \"and for a swelling (שְׂאֵת) and for a scab (סַפַּחַת) and for a bright spot (בַּהֶרֶת)\" — these are the first plagues with which He opened (Leviticus 13:2): \"When a man shall have in the skin of his flesh,\" etc. And in every place He places the בַּהֶרֶת last, because it is the most intense and the severest of them all."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:53:56.507158048Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}